<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">François Guizot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1787–1874</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">François Guizot was a French historian and liberal politician who dominated the government of the July Monarchy in the 1840s, first as foreign minister and then as prime minister. As education minister his law of 1833 required every commune to keep a primary school. His refusal to widen the narrow electorate helped bring the revolution of February 1848 and the king's fall.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francois-guizot.jpg" alt="François Guizot" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jehan Georges Vibert / After Paul Delaroche · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guizot,_Fran%C3%A7ois_-_2_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
